<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Vilnius (1561)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1561">1561</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Pacta subiectionis · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-war">Livonian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vilnius">Vilnius</a>, or Pacta subiectionis, was concluded on 28 November 1561 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigismund-ii-augustus">Sigismund II Augustus</a>, king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and grand duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>, and the Livonian Order and the Archbishopric of Riga. Facing Russian invasion during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-war">Livonian War</a>, the order was secularised: its lands south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-dvina">Daugava</a> became the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/courland">Courland</a> and Semigallia under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gotthard-kettler">Gotthard Kettler</a>, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonia">Livonia</a> proper passed to Lithuania.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-vilnius-1561.jpg" alt="Treaty of Vilnius (1561)" width="300" height="476" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pacta_subiectionis_v%C4%81ciskais_tulkojums.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
